From 75a3de27d8fa0579f4d136ac5641adf9cb076d78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 11:21:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stage 282: the tie is not the probe's business

Two runs settle it. The return path was supposed to break ties invented
by retrieval pollution; at one witness the teacher resolved 45% of the
held-out ties and its ceiling fell to 0.445, at two witnesses it resolved
fewer and reached 0.533 - still below the 0.594 it scores with the probe
switched off entirely. A tied address has no settled value, so every
resolution can only be wrong, and the pollution the rule was written for
has largely gone since --subject-filter started matching case.

So a tie is a conflict again, without asking. The probe keeps the job it
demonstrably does: on the lead it is worth +0.030 reward and +0.022
accuracy on held-out, +0.018 and +0.016 on the training tape, with clean
answers at 1.000 against 0.960 without it. --tie-probe restores the
two-witness rule, since that is the arm these numbers came from and it
should stay runnable rather than only described.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PGuqHAMhjCxVAADm3R4wxK
